  "date": "20260914",
  "note": "Durable, tracked preservation of one genuine bounded ZTH supervised-capability-loop run of the reviewed_v1 current-vs-superseded (temporal-reconciliation) task. The 1.7B worker produced well-formed exact_json on all four attempts (4/4 valid JSON) and matched the expected answer on none (0/4 exact): S1 superseded correct every time; S2 current (expected superseded); S3 superseded (expected current); S4 flipped; pivotal_commit never the invariant-establishing 47cf409 (worker chose 002a1b7 then 7c68f2b). The genuine temporal/causal reconciliation weakness is preserved verbatim in genuine_raw_evidence. The two 27B local-teacher artifacts (local-teacher-{1,2}.json) are reclassified in README.md from a model-capability failure to a CONFIG/OMISSION failure: the loop invoked the teacher with no request_policy_name and ICM_QWEN3_8_27B_REQUEST_POLICY unset, so resolve_worker_spec resolved resolved_request_policy_name=None and bound no policy (request_provenance shows thinking_budget_tokens:null, chat_template_kwargs:null). Unbounded reasoning then consumed the whole 1200-token max_tokens budget in the reasoning channel (finish_reason:length, status:reasoning_only, completion_tokens:1200), truncating the structured JSON; the 27B reasoning channel nonetheless derived the correct pivotal commit 47cf409, so the model was capable and the request configuration was not. Fixed by the default-routine guard in icm_spec.py:resolve_worker_spec (explicit arg > env var > routine). Terminal review state is infrastructure_error (external teacher unconfigured: ZTH_EXTERNAL_TEACHER_COMMAND not set), which masked the worker verdict and is not a model verdict. See README.md and genuine_raw_evidence/NOTE.md.",
